{"tool_name":"saige","contents":["oeb","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"saige","home":"https://github.com/weizhouUMICH/SAIGE","summary":"SAIGE is an R package with Scalable and Accurate Implementation of Generalized mixed model. It accounts for sample relatedness and is feasible for genetic association tests in large cohorts and biobanks (N > 400,000).\n\nSAIGE performs single-variant association tests for binary traits and quantitative traits. For binary traits, SAIGE uses the saddlepoint approximation (SPA)(mhof, J. P. , 1961; Kuonen, D. 1999; Dey, R. et.al 2017) to account for case-control imbalance.\n\nSAIGE-GENE (implemented in the SAIGE R package) performs gene- or region-based association tests (Burde, SKAT, SKAT-O) for binary traits and quantitative traits. Note: SAIGE-GENE accounts for case-control imbalance in gene-based tests (>= 0.35.8.5)","addition_date":"2021-07-08T20:06:20Z","last_update_date":"2021-07-08T20:06:20Z","biotools_curie":"biotools:saige","edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2928"}]}],"name":"SAIGE","owner":"leipzig"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:saige/undefined/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":null,"interpreted":null,"license":null,"public":true,"readme":false,"repository":{"anonymous":null,"online":null}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[],"readme":false,"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"operational":200,"ssl":true,"ssl_err":null}},"support":{"issue_tracking":{"public_tracker":null,"resolve_time":null}}},{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/bioconda:saige:0.35.8.8/cmd